    "name": "Soft-neck Garlic ( CA )",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Softneck garlic is&nbsp;a common garlic variety known for its mild flavor, long storage life, and pliable neck, which makes it ideal for braiding. It's best suited for warmer climates with mild winters, though it can be grown in colder zones with proper mulching. This type is popular in grocery stores and is generally easy for both beginner and experienced gardeners to grow.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by: Christopher Ranch located in California</span></p>",
